+# ✅ Offline Status Integration Complete!

+The `OfflineStatusIndicator` has been successfully added to your key screens. Here's what's been
+implemented:
+
+## Screens Updated
+
+The offline status indicator is now showing on these main screens:
+
+### ✅ **OngoingProjectsScreen**
+
+- Shows connection status and pending sync items
+- Located at the top of the projects list
+
+### ✅ **AddTaskScreen**
+
+- Displays sync status when creating new tasks
+- Shows at the top of the form
+
+### ✅ **AddProjectScreen**
+
+- Indicates connection status during project creation
+- Positioned at the beginning of the content
+
+### ✅ **TaskDetailScreen**
+
+- Shows offline status and pending changes for task details
+- Placed at the top of the task information
+
+### ✅ **CompletedProjectsScreen**
+
+- Displays connection status for completed projects view
+- Located at the top of the screen
+
+### ✅ **ProjectDetailScreen**
+
+- Shows sync status for project details and tasks
+- Positioned at the beginning of the content area
+
+### ✅ **ProfileScreen**
+
+- Indicates connection status on the profile page
+- Placed at the top of the profile information
+
+## What Users Will See
+
+The indicator shows different states:
+
+### **Online State**
+
+- Green WiFi icon
+- "Online" text
+- Shows pending sync count if any items need syncing
+
+### **Offline State**
+
+- Orange cloud-off icon
+- "Offline" text
+- Shows number of changes pending sync
+
+### **Connection Issues**
+
+- Red sync-problem icon
+- "Losing Connection" text
+- Indicates unstable network
+
+## Example Usage
+
+If you want to add the indicator to any other screen, simply import and use:
+
+```kotlin
+import kv.apps.taskmanager.presentation.components.OfflineStatusIndicator
+
+@Composable
+fun YourScreen() {
+ Column {
+ // Add at the top of your screen content
+ OfflineStatusIndicator(
+ modifier = Modifier
+ .fillMaxWidth()
+ .padding(horizontal = 16.dp, vertical = 8.dp)
+ )
+ 
+ // Your existing screen content...
+ }
+}
+```
+
+## Real-time Updates
+
+The indicator automatically:
+
+- ✅ **Monitors network connectivity** in real-time
+- ✅ **Counts pending sync items** every 5 seconds
+- ✅ **Updates UI immediately** when connection changes
+- ✅ **Shows sync progress** when items are being synchronized
+
+## User Benefits
+
+Your users now get:
+
+1. **Immediate Feedback**: Know instantly if they're online or offline
+2. **Sync Awareness**: See exactly how many changes are pending sync
+3. **Confidence**: Work offline knowing their changes are safely stored
+4. **Transparency**: Clear indication of app status at all times
+
+## ️ Technical Implementation
+
+The `OfflineStatusIndicator` uses:
+
+- **Hilt Dependency Injection** for seamless integration
+- **StateFlow** for reactive state management
+- **Room Database** queries for sync status
+- **Network Connectivity Observer** for real-time network monitoring
+
+## Next Steps
+
+The offline-first system is now fully integrated! Your users can:
+
+- Work seamlessly offline on projects and tasks
+- See real-time sync status across all screens
+- Get visual feedback about their connection state
+- Trust that their work is always saved locally
+
+The indicator will automatically appear on all the screens listed above, providing users with
+constant awareness of their app's connectivity and sync status.
+
+---
+
+**Your Task Manager app now provides a world-class offline-first experience! **
